    thinking: "**Examining Potential Defects**\n\nI\'ve started by examining the app\'s components, focusing on potential defects. I\'ve discovered empty metadata entries for the app name and description in `metadata.json`. I\'m also looking at the placeholder product images; all products currently use them. Now I\'ll proceed with looking closely at the overall structure!\n\n\n**Addressing Placeholder Issues**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the use of placeholder images, and found they\'re used extensively, even in mock order generation. Specifically, `server.ts` and `OrderHistory.tsx` use placeholder text-based URLs instead of actual images. Moreover, the in-memory mock database presents an issue; creating and submitting orders doesn\'t persist, or even clear the cart! Static hardcoded values for price calculations are also a defect. The comparison feature also needs to be examined.\n\n\n**Pinpointing UI Interaction Gaps**\n\nI\'ve discovered critical UI interaction gaps. The \"\330\247\331\201\330\262\331\210\330\257\331\206 \330\250\331\207 \330\263\330\250\330\257\" button lacks an `onClick` handler, preventing product additions to the cart. Similarly, the compare icon in `ProductDetail.tsx` is non-functional, as it lacks the handler calls. I\'m now reviewing review persistence in `ProductReviews.tsx` and evaluating the static pages, while I check how search and filters work. I am also investigating the dark mode compatibility on various pages.\n\n\n"
