  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Website Flaws**\n\nI\'m focusing now on a comprehensive analysis of the identified website issues. My goal is to structure a detailed audit in Persian, encompassing all bugs, UX gaps, and areas for improvement. I\'m aiming for clarity and completeness in the final report.\n\n\n**Addressing Key Website Deficiencies**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the website\'s critical flaws. The `metadata.json` file is empty, causing default values. Placeholder images and hardcoded product data in `server.ts` and `OrderHistory.tsx` lack realism. A major issue is the hardcoded order summary in `Checkout.tsx`, severing the checkout process from the actual cart state. I\'m prioritizing these three aspects for an in-depth Persian audit.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Systemic Failures**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on critical system failures. Clicking \"Submit Order & Pay\" triggers a Toast message and profile redirection, but neither saves the order to history nor clears the cart. The \"Add to Cart\" button in Compare.tsx has no handler, and the comparison icon in ProductDetail.tsx is not linked to any compare list. I\'ll translate these insights into a detailed report in Persian.\n\n\n**Evaluating Dark Mode Issues**\n\nI\'m presently tackling inconsistencies with the dark mode implementation. Specifically, files like `Checkout.tsx`, parts of `ProductDetail.tsx`, and `Cart.tsx` are using static classes without dark mode counterparts, leading to visual disharmony. Additionally, I\'m noting the absence of database connection and persistent data storage. Next, I\'ll integrate these aspects into the audit.\n\n\n"
