    thinking: "**Identifying Website Issues**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a comprehensive list forming based on the first prompt! I\'ve broken down all the potential flaws of the website across many features like persistence, SEO, and RTL support. Core features, search, and checkout all have clear problems. Cart/wishlist shortcomings are also there.\n\n\n**Planning the Fixes**\n\nI am now organizing the identified issues into a comprehensive plan for complete resolution, aiming for a clean fix without introducing new problems. I\'m focusing on RTL direction, typography, and font support within the `index.html`, `metadata.json`, and `index.css` files, specifically ensuring Persian font setup (like Vazirmatn or system fonts with RTL font family stack) alongside `dir=\"rtl\"` and an accurate Persian document title. The goal is a perfect and complete fix.\n\n\n**Addressing Data Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on data persistence across multiple contexts. I\'ve noted that `CartContext.tsx`, `WishlistContext.tsx`, and `CompareContext.tsx` all utilize `useState` without `localStorage` initialization, meaning a refresh clears the data, a critical flaw. Also, I\'m checking the robustness of `OrderHistory.tsx`\'s `localStorage` usage, along with verifying `ProductReviews.tsx`\'s storage method.\n\n\n**Validating Order Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a complete order details view. I\'m verifying the inclusion of all vital information. Applied discounts, shipping costs, delivery address, tracking numbers, timestamps, and other specifics need to be accounted for.\n\n**Checking Stock and Quantities**\n\nI\'m now going into stock validation. For `ProductCard.tsx`, `ProductDetail.tsx`, and `Cart.tsx`, I\'m double-checking how the code handles product stock limits. I need to make sure out-of-stock items, which I\'m calling \"\331\206\330\247\331\205\331\210\330\254\331\210\330\257\", are handled correctly. Plus, users should only be able to increment quantities up to the stock limit.\n\n**Reviewing Search and Categories**\n\nNow I\'m making sure filtering, sorting, and search work just right. Specifically, `Products.tsx` and `HeaderSearch.tsx`. The goal is to make sure URL parameters are in sync with state in category filtering, price ranges, ratings, and sort orders. A search history also needs to be implemented.\n\n\n"
